You are wrong, as usual. 

Speed boots _are_ faster than the wand, but speed boots _plus_ the wand
are as fast as speed boots alone.
Eating a Q, /oSpeed, a divine blessing or gaining XL as certain classes
all give you "fast" speed. Speed boots give you "very fast" speed. So do
!oSpeed and +oHaste, but only temporarily. "Fast" means 1/3 faster than
normal. "Very fast" means 2/3 faster than normal. Having both "fast" and
"very fast", (e.g., zapping yourself with a /oSpeed, then quaffing the
potion) means you're still only "very fast", and 2/3 faster than normal,
not twice as fast.

